ch transfer all the documents  and reports required  are transferred to our manufacturing  site via our dedicated tt team  a single batch of adsorbent is produced  at the same  or larger scale than the verification  batches  the dt batch is fully evaluated and  assessed for comparability  to that of the verification batches for  the case study  an sds page of the tech transfer batch  was performed  and demonstrated comparability to the  verification batches  with a strong main target band visible  once the tech transfer batch has been  fully evaluated  manufacturer will commence creating at  least three  validation batches  during tech transfer and at the start of  manufacture  the equipment requirements and user  requirement specifications are evaluated  the incoming raw materials in process  assays  and final product assays for the product  are assessed for their suitability  and validated ligand and adsorbent  synthesis methods are validated  and all required standard operating  procedures and badge manufacturing  records  are established validation of the  adsorbent synthesis  is usually performed with the  manufacture of a minimum  of three batches usually at a larger  scale to that of the tt batch  demonstrating comparability and quality  the custom adsorbent is now a fully  validated and supported product  and can be supplied to the customer  however to fully support and enable the  customer  estrella also offers a column packing  service  if this is desired a packing development  program is initiated  to fully understand the packing  properties of the absorbent  and define all the parameters required  to produce  a uniform and robust packing process  this method follows the same route once  again  back through tech transfer and into  manufacture  along with our external testing  including transportation testing  we ensure that we can deliver a  plug-and-play play product  to the customer estrella also provide  smaller lab scale columns to perform  screening 